## **2. Table Definitions**

### **2.1. `roles`**

> Manages user roles as data rather than code to ensure clarity and scalability.

| Column Name | Data Type | Constraints | Description |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `id` | INT | PRIMARY KEY | Unique identifier for roles (0: fan, 1: band_member, 2: admin) |
| `name` | TEXT | UNIQUE, NOT NULL | Role name ('fan', 'band_member', 'admin') |

### **2.2. `profiles`**

> Basic profile information for all users who have joined the service. Connected 1:1 with auth.users.

| Column Name | Data Type | Constraints | Description |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `id` | UUID | PRIMARY KEY, FK (auth.users), ON DELETE CASCADE | Unique ID of Supabase authenticated user. Profile automatically deleted when authentication info is deleted. |
| `username` | TEXT | UNIQUE, NOT NULL | Unique nickname set by the user |
| `role_id` | INT | NOT NULL, DEFAULT 0, FK (roles.id) | User's role ID. References `roles` table. |
| `image_url` | TEXT |  | User's profile image URL |

### **2.3. `bands`**

> Unique information for all indie bands registered in the service.

| Column Name | Data Type | Constraints | Description |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `id` | SERIAL | PRIMARY KEY | Band's unique identifier (auto-increment) |
| `owner_id` | UUID | FK (profiles.id), ON DELETE SET NULL | Profile ID of the owner who created the band. Band is maintained when owner leaves. |
| `band_name` | TEXT | NOT NULL | Official name of the band |
| `created_at` | TIMESTAMPTZ | DEFAULT NOW() | Time when band information was created |

### **2.4. `band_members`**

> Junction table defining which users are members of which bands.

| Column Name | Data Type | Constraints | Description |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `id` | SERIAL | PRIMARY KEY | Unique identifier for the relationship |
| `band_id` | INT | NOT NULL, FK (bands.id), ON DELETE CASCADE | ID of the band the member belongs to. Member info automatically deleted when band is deleted. |
| `profile_id` | UUID | NOT NULL, FK (profiles.id), ON DELETE CASCADE | Profile ID of the member. Relationship automatically deleted when member leaves. |
| `position` | TEXT |  | Position within the band (e.g., 'Vocalist', 'Guitarist') |

### **2.5. `subscriptions`**

> Junction table defining which fans are subscribed to which bands.

| Column Name | Data Type | Constraints | Description |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `fan_id` | UUID | PRIMARY KEY, FK (profiles.id), ON DELETE CASCADE | Profile ID of the subscribing fan. Subscription info automatically deleted when fan leaves. |
| `band_id` | INT | PRIMARY KEY, FK (bands.id), ON DELETE CASCADE | ID of the subscribed band. Subscription info automatically deleted when band is deleted. |
| `subscribed_at` | TIMESTAMPTZ | DEFAULT NOW() | Time when subscription started |

### **2.6. `stories`**

> Stores story information posted by band members.

| Column Name | Data Type | Constraints | Description |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `id` | SERIAL | PRIMARY KEY | Unique identifier for the story |
| `member_id` | INT | NOT NULL, FK (band_members.id), ON DELETE CASCADE | ID of the member who posted the story. Story automatically deleted when member relationship is deleted. |
| `media_url` | TEXT | NOT NULL | URL of the media file |
| `media_type` | TEXT | NOT NULL | Media type ('image' or 'video') |
| `created_at` | TIMESTAMPTZ | DEFAULT NOW() | Time when story was created |

### **2.7. `schedules`**

> Stores official schedule information for bands.

| Column Name | Data Type | Constraints | Description |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `id` | SERIAL | PRIMARY KEY | Unique identifier for the schedule |
| `band_id` | INT | NOT NULL, FK (bands.id), ON DELETE CASCADE | ID of the band hosting the schedule. Schedule automatically deleted when band is deleted. |
| `title` | TEXT | NOT NULL | Title of the schedule |
| `event_date` | DATE | NOT NULL | Event date |
| `location` | TEXT |  | Event location |
| `ticket_link` | TEXT |  | Ticket booking URL |
| `created_at` | TIMESTAMPTZ | DEFAULT NOW() | Time when schedule was registered |

### **2.8. `goods_posts`**

> Stores post information for the goods community.

| Column Name | Data Type | Constraints | Description |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `id` | SERIAL | PRIMARY KEY | Unique identifier for the post |
| `author_id` | UUID | NOT NULL, FK (profiles.id), ON DELETE CASCADE | Author's profile ID. Post automatically deleted when author leaves. |
| `title` | TEXT | NOT NULL | Title of the post |
| `content` | TEXT |  | Content of the post |
| `image_url` | TEXT |  | Attached image URL |
| `created_at` | TIMESTAMPTZ | DEFAULT NOW() | Time when post was created |

---

## **3. Indexing Strategy**

To optimize read operation performance, indexes are created on foreign key columns frequently used in `WHERE` clauses or `JOIN` conditions.

- `idx_profiles_role_id`: Improves performance for user queries by role
- `idx_bands_owner_id`: Improves performance for querying bands by specific owner
- `idx_band_members_band_id`, `idx_band_members_profile_id`: Improves performance for querying members of specific bands or bands belonging to specific members
- `idx_subscriptions_band_id`: Improves performance for querying subscribers of specific bands
- `idx_stories_member_id`: Improves performance for querying stories by specific members
- `idx_schedules_band_id`: Improves performance for querying schedules of specific bands
- `idx_goods_posts_author_id`: Improves performance for querying posts by specific authors

This document defines the Supabase Postgres database schema for the 'Indie Band' service. It aims to ensure data consistency and integrity by describing the purpose of each table, column details, and relationships between tables.